This is a miscompilation bug in ValueTracking.
Issue title: [InstCombine] fcmp is incorrectly inverted
Detailed information:
BUG TYPE:
    miscompilation

VERIFICATION RESULT:
    Invalid refinement in @test_select_nnan_nsz_fcmp_olt -- Value mismatch

VIOLATED PROPERTY:
    return-value equality

SOURCE (pre-transformation IR):
define float @test_select_nnan_nsz_fcmp_olt(float %x) {
  %cmp = fcmp olt float %x, 0.000000e+00
  %sel = select nnan i1 %cmp, float %x, float -0.000000e+00
  ret float %sel
}

TARGET (post-transformation IR):
; ModuleID = '<stdin>'
source_filename = "<stdin>"

define float @test_select_nnan_nsz_fcmp_olt(float %x) {
  %.inv = fcmp oge float %x, 0.000000e+00
  %sel1 = select i1 %.inv, float -0.000000e+00, float %x
  ret float %sel1
}

WHAT THE TRANSFORMATION CHANGED:
  only in target:
    %.inv: %.inv = fcmp oge float %x, 0.000000e+00
    %sel1: %sel1 = select i1 %.inv, float -0.000000e+00, float %x
  only in source:
    %cmp: %cmp = fcmp olt float %x, 0.000000e+00
    %sel: %sel = select nnan i1 %cmp, float %x, float -0.000000e+00

CRITICAL VALUES:
    %.inv
    %cmp
    %sel
    %sel1

DEPENDENCY CHAIN (source):
    %cmp = fcmp olt float %x, 0.000000e+00
    %sel = select nnan i1 %cmp, float %x, float -0.000000e+00

CONTROL FLOW (blocks entered by the failing execution):
    (none)

COUNTEREXAMPLE INPUT:
    float %x = #x7f800004 (SNaN)

DIVERGENCE (source vs target on that input):
    %.inv: source = (not computed)   target = #x0 (0)
    %sel1: source = (not computed)   target = #x7f800004 (SNaN)

INTERPRETATION:
    A transformation must preserve the returned value for every input on which the source is well-defined.
    On the input above the source yields #x80000000 (-0.0) while the target yields #x7f800004 (SNaN).
    The earliest reported divergence is at %.inv.

